update public.species set body = $v$A peaceful algae- and detritus-eater popular for ponds and coldwater tanks, since it tolerates low temperatures well. It gives birth to live young slowly, so populations stay manageable. The 'trapdoor' operculum seals its shell when threatened. Keep pH at 7 or above with some hardness (GH 6 or more) so the shell stays smooth and strong, and avoid copper medications, which kill snails.$v$ where slug = $v$japanese-trapdoor-snail$v$;
