update public.species set ph_min = 5.5, body = $v$Needs soft, acidic water, ideally tinted with leaf litter or peat, to thrive and show color. In the wild they live in peat swamps where the water can be as acidic as pH 4.5; in the aquarium aim for pH 5.5 to 6.5. Keep a school of 6 or more with dim lighting and plenty of plants. Much calmer than most barbs and a good fit with small peaceful fish.$v$ where slug = $v$snakeskin-barb$v$;
