update public.species set ph_min = 5.5, body = $v$Needs very soft, acidic blackwater with leaf litter, dim light and small caves. In the wild they live in peat swamp water as low as pH 4.5; in the aquarium aim for about pH 5.5 to 6.5. Best kept as a pair or small group in a species tank since it is shy and easily outcompeted. Feed small live and frozen foods; many refuse flakes.$v$ where slug = $v$licorice-gourami$v$;
update public.species set temp_max_f = 82, min_tank_gal = 55, body = $v$Grows to around 8 inches, so plan on 55 gallons or more. Very peaceful and hardy, and even males are rarely aggressive. Good with medium community fish; avoid nippers that target its long ventral feelers.$v$ where slug = $v$snakeskin-gourami$v$;
