update public.species set ph_min = 7.8, ph_max = 8.6, body = $v$Young duboisi are black with bright white polka dots; adults turn dark with a blue face and a single yellow or white band. Like all Tropheus they eat algae and need a high-fiber, plant-based diet, because rich, meaty foods can cause deadly bloat. They're quarrelsome with their own kind, so they're kept in large groups of ten or more to spread the aggression, in hard, alkaline water with lots of rockwork. Duboisi are a bit milder than many Tropheus, which makes them a good first Tropheus for keepers ready for the commitment.$v$ where slug = $v$tropheus-duboisi$v$;
