update public.species set ph_min = 5.5, gh_min = 1, body = $v$Scarlet bettas are a wild betta from blackwater peat swamps, small and slender compared to the domestic betta. They're deep wine red, and many show a shining green spot on each side. They need very soft, acidic water. In the wild their water can be as low as pH 4; in the aquarium aim for about pH 5.5 to 6.5, which most keepers reach with RO water, peat and leaf litter. Keep a pair or a small group in a quiet, dim, heavily planted tank with a tight lid. Feed small live and frozen foods; many won't take dry food at first.$v$ where slug = $v$scarlet-betta$v$;
